{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he delivered me from the sword of Pharaoh.</b> For at the birth of Eliezer, that king of Egypt who pursued Moses had already died, as it says: וַיְהִי בַיָּמִים הָהֵם וַיָּמָת מֶלֶךְ מִצְרַיִם (Exodus 2:23). Then he could trust that he would escape the sword of Pharaoh, for until his death Moses was not safe from his sword in any place where he might become known to Pharaoh — as in the matter of אִם יֵשׁ גּוֹי וּמַמְלָכָה אֲשֶׁר לֹא שָׁלַח אֲדֹנִי שָׁם לְבַקֶּשְׁךָ וְהִשְׁבִּיעַ אֶת הַמַּמְלָכָה וְאֶת הַגּוֹי (1 Kings 18:10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:02.059597416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}